    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">That which allows how organisations cooperate to achieve their mutually agreed goals. It can be capabilities, forces, or resources.

Source: Based on the Black's Law Dictionary definition of enablers and the EIRA definition of organisational interoperability.
&lt;a href=&quot;https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/eia/document/how-does-eira-support-interoperability&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/eia/document/how-does-eira-support-in…&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;http://thelawdictionary.org/enablers/&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;http://thelawdictionary.org/enablers/&lt;/a&gt;

