  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DataCatalogTechnologyService">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Definition: Data Catalog ABB is a Technology Service that enables the procedures of a centralised metadata repository to provide information about the data assets in a public administration

Source: Inspired in JRC

Source reference: &lt;a href=&quot;https://data.jrc.ec.europa.eu/about&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://data.jrc.ec.europa.eu/about&lt;/a&gt;

Example: The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Jount Research Centre Data Catalogue. &lt;a href=&quot;https://data.jrc.ec.europa.eu/&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://data.jrc.ec.europa.eu/&lt;/a&gt;

LOST view: Technical view - Infrastructure

Interoperability saliency: Data Catalog ABB is salient for semantic interoperability because it provides grouped datasets of information enhanced with metadata to promote their discovery, sharing and understanding for other digital services and public administrations

Identifier: &lt;a href=&quot;http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DataCatalogTechnologyService&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DataCatalogTechnologyService&lt;/a&gt;

