  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DataManagementEnablersGrouping">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Definition: Data Management Enablers ABB is a Grouping that refers to components and services that support effective data management practices and procedures.

Source: Inspired in European Comision- Data Governance and data policies at the European Comission

Source reference: &lt;a href=&quot;https://commission.europa.eu/publications/data-governance-and-data-policies-european-commission_en&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://commission.europa.eu/publications/data-governance-and-data-poli…&lt;/a&gt;

Example: The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Context Broker as a CEF Building Block. &lt;a href=&quot;https://ec.europa.eu/digital-building-blocks/wikis/download/attachments/82773424/Context%20Broker%20Brochure.pdf?version=1&amp;amp;modificationDate=1558016168498&amp;amp;api=v2&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://ec.europa.eu/digital-building-blocks/wikis/download/attachments…&lt;/a&gt;

IoP Dimension: Structural IoP, Behavioral IoP

LOST view: Technical view - application

Interoperability saliency: The Data Management Enablers Grouping ABB is salient for technical interoperability because it comprises the tools, components and services related to data management. Data Management Enablers are relevant as they support effective and efficient data management, ensuring that interoperability can be achieved between digital public services.

eira:ID: &lt;a href=&quot;http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DataManagementEnablersGrouping&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DataManagementEnablersGrouping&lt;/a&gt;

ABB name: eira:DataManagementEnablersGrouping

EIRA concept: eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock

eiraPURI: &lt;a href=&quot;http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DataManagementEnablersGrouping&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DataManagementEnablersGrouping&lt;/a&gt;</skos:definition>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Data Management Enablers</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/view/TechnicalView-Application"/>
    <ns0:properties rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">{&quot;namespaces&quot;:{&quot;rdf&quot;:{&quot;namespace&quot;:&quot;rdf:&quot;,&quot;uri&quot;:&quot;http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1999\/02\/22-rdf-syntax-ns#&quot;},&quot;skos&quot;:{&quot;namespace&quot;:&quot;skos:&quot;,&quot;uri&quot;:&quot;http:\/\/www.w3.org\/2004\/02\/skos\/core#&quot;},&quot;dct&quot;:{&quot;namespace&quot;:&quot;dct:&quot;,&quot;uri&quot;:&quot;http:\/\/purl.org\/dc\/terms\/&quot;},&quot;eira&quot;:{&quot;namespace&quot;:&quot;eira:&quot;,&quot;uri&quot;:&quot;http:\/\/data.europa.eu\/dr8\/&quot;}},&quot;rows&quot;:[{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;rdf:type&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;http:\/\/www.w3.org\/2004\/02\/skos\/core#Concept&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;skos:notation&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;Properties of Data Management Enablers&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;dct:identifier&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;http:\/\/data.europa.eu\/dr8\/DataManagementEnablersGrouping_Properties&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;dct:identifier&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;http:\/\/data.europa.eu\/dr8\/DataManagementEnablersGrouping&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;skos:prefLabel&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;Properties of Data Management Enablers&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;dct:type&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;eira:DataManagementEnablersGrouping&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;dct:modified&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;2023-05-25&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;skos:definition&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;Data Management Enablers ABB is a Grouping that refers to components and services that support effective data management practices and procedures.&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:definitionSource&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;Inspired in European Comision- Data Governance and data policies at the European Comission&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:definitionSourceReference&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;https:\/\/commission.europa.eu\/publications\/data-governance-and-data-policies-european-commission_en&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;skos:example&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Context Broker as a CEF Building Block. https:\/\/ec.europa.eu\/digital-building-blocks\/wikis\/download\/attachments\/82773424\/Context%20Broker%20Brochure.pdf?version=1\u0026modificationDate=1558016168498\u0026api=v2&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:iopSaliency&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;The Data Management Enablers Grouping ABB is salient for technical interoperability because it comprises the tools, components and services related to data management. Data Management Enablers are relevant as they support effective and efficient data management, ensuring that interoperability can be achieved between digital public services.&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:concept&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:PURI&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;http:\/\/data.europa.eu\/dr8\/DataManagementEnablersGrouping&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:iopDimension&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;Structural IoP&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:iopDimension&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;Behavioral IoP&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:view&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;Technical view - application&quot;}]}</ns0:properties>
    <skos:related>
      <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DataVirtualizationApplicationComponent">
        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Definition: Data Virtualization ABB is an Application Component that implements the functionality of retrieving and manipulating data without requiring technical details about the data format or location.

Source: Joinup

Source reference: &lt;a href=&quot;https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/inline-files/Data%20visualisation%20service%20definition.pdf&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/inline-files/Data%20vis…&lt;/a&gt;

Example: The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Virtuoso. Virtuoso Universal Server is modern platform built on existing open standards that harnesses the power of Hyperlinks (functioning as Super Keys) for breaking down data silos that impede both user and enterprise ability. For example, Virtuoso's core SQL &amp;amp; SPARQL powers many Enterprise Knowledge Graph initiatives just as it does DBpedia and a majority of nodes in the Linked Open Data Cloud -- the world's largest publicly accessible Knowledge Graph. &lt;a href=&quot;https://big-data-test-infrastructure.ec.europa.eu/service-offering/virtuoso_en&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://big-data-test-infrastructure.ec.europa.eu/service-offering/virt…&lt;/a&gt;

IoP Dimension: Structural IoP

LOST view: Technical view - application

Interoperability saliency: The Data Virtualization Component ABB is salient for technical interoperability because it realises the services established and defined by the Data Virtualization Service ABB, collaborating with enabling interoperability between public services that generate, process or consume data.

Identifier: &lt;a href=&quot;http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DataVirtualizationApplicationComponent&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DataVirtualizationApplicationComponent&lt;/a&gt;

eira:ID: &lt;a href=&quot;http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DataVirtualizationApplicationComponent&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DataVirtualizationApplicationComponent&lt;/a&gt;

ABB name: eira:DataVirtualizationApplicationComponent

EIRA concept: eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2022-23-01</skos:definition>
