ion contains a full description of the architectural decisions.&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;skos:definition&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;An Architectural Decision Record (ADR) is a document that captures the key decisions made during the architectural design and development of a software system. It is used to record the rationale, alternatives considered, and trade-offs made during the decision-making process, as well as the context and implications of each decision.&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:definitionSource&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;Architectural Decision Records&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:definitionSourceReference&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;https:\/\/adr.github.io\/&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:adr_context&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;The context explains why we need to make a decision. It also describes the alternatives along with the pros and cons.&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:adr_decision&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;The decision describes the justification for why the particular solution was accepted. It has more emphasis on the why rather than the how.&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:adr_status&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;[Proposed (under review)|Accepted (approved and ready for implementation)|Superseded (superseded by another decision)]&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:adr_consecuences&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;The consequences section contains information about the overall impact of an architectural decision. Every decision has trade-offs. That\u2019s why it\u2019s crucial to include the analysis to provide a clear picture.&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:iopDimension&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;Governance IoP&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:view&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;Interoperability Motivation View&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:concept&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock&quot;}]}</ns0:properties>
