  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EuropeanDIgitalSovereignty">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">DEFINITION:
European digital sovereignty ABB is a Principle entailing the ensurance that all underlying digital components of ICT solutions (hardware, software, and services) meet European requirements, including the requirements to deploy a secure cloud infrastructure and interoperable services that fully comply with European legal provisions and ethical values.

Source: Europarl
(&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.europarl.europa.eu/RegData/etudes/BRIE/2020/651992/EPRS_BRI(2020)651992_EN.pdf#:~:text=The%20notion%20of%20%27technological%27%20or%20%27digital%20sovereignty%27%20has,ability%20to%20act%20independently%20in%20the%20digital%20world2&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://www.europarl.europa.eu/RegData/etudes/BRIE/2020/651992/EPRS_BRI…&lt;/a&gt;)

EXAMPLES:
The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB):</skos:definition>
