  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/IntegrityVerificationApplicationService">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Definition: Integrity Verification ABB is an Application Service that enables the procedures to ensure that information has not been altered in an unauthorized manner since it was created, transmitted or stored.

Source: CSRC

Source reference: &lt;a href=&quot;https://csrc.nist.gov/glossary/term/integrity_verification&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://csrc.nist.gov/glossary/term/integrity_verification&lt;/a&gt;

Example: The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): WITDOM’s Integrity and Consistency Verification component protects the integrity and consistency of data outsourced to an untrusted remote storage. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cyberwatching.eu/projects/1006/witdom/products/witdom-integrity-and-consistency-verification&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://www.cyberwatching.eu/projects/1006/witdom/products/witdom-integ…&lt;/a&gt;

IoP Dimension: Behavioral IoP

LOST view: Technical view - application

Interoperability saliency: The Integrity Verification Application Service ABB is salient for interoperability because is a key service to ensure data integrity, it can perform checks on: changes on the data, if changes are authorised or not, and when those changes have been performed. By ensuring this, digital public services can provide additional trust in the data and information provided to stakeholders.

Identifier: &lt;a href=&quot;http://data.europa.eu/dr8/IntegrityVerificationApplicationService&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;http://data.europa.eu/dr8/IntegrityVerificationApplicationService&lt;/a&gt;

eira:ID: ABB621

ABB name: eira:IntegrityVerificationApplicationService

EIRA concept: eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2022-20-01</skos:definition>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Integrity Verification</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/viewpoint/InteroperabilitySecurityViewpoint"/>
    <ns0:properties rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">{&quot;namespaces&quot;:{&quot;rdf&quot;:{&quot;namespace&quot;:&quot;rdf:&quot;,&quot;uri&quot;:&quot;http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1999\/02\/22-rdf-syntax-ns#&quot;},&quot;skos&quot;:{&quot;namespace&quot;:&quot;skos:&quot;,&quot;uri&quot;:&quot;http:\/\/www.w3.org\/2004\/02\/skos\/core#&quot;},&quot;dct&quot;:{&quot;namespace&quot;:&quot;dct:&quot;,&quot;uri&quot;:&quot;http:\/\/purl.org\/dc\/terms\/&quot;},&quot;eira&quot;:{&quot;namespace&quot;:&quot;eira:&quot;,&quot;uri&quot;:&quot;http:\/\/data.europa.eu\/dr8\/&quot;}},&quot;rows&quot;:[{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;rdf:type&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;http:\/\/www.w3.org\/2004\/02\/skos\/core#Concept&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;skos:notation&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;Properties of Integrity Verification&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;dct:identifier&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;http:\/\/data.europa.eu\/dr8\/IntegrityVerificationApplicationService_Properties&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;dct:identifier&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;http:\/\/data.europa.eu\/dr8\/IntegrityVerificationApplicationService&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;skos:prefLabel&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;Properties of Integrity Verification&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:PURI&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;http:\/\/data.europa.eu\/dr8\/IntegrityVerificationApplicationService&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;dct:type&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;eira:IntegrityVerificationApplicationService&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;dct:modified&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;2022-01-20&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;skos:definition&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;Integrity Verification ABB is an Application Service that enables the procedures to ensure that information has not been altered in an unauthorized manner since it was created, transmitted or stored.&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:definitionSource&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;CSRC&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:definitionSourceReference&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;https:\/\/csrc.nist.gov\/glossary\/term\/integrity_verification&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;skos:example&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): WITDOM\u2019s Integrity and Consistency Verification component protects the integrity and consistency of data outsourced to an untrusted remote storage. https:\/\/www.cyberwatching.eu\/projects\/1006\/witdom\/products\/witdom-integrity-and-consistency-verification&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:iopSaliency&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;The Integrity Verification Application Service ABB is salient for interoperability because is a key service to ensure data integrity, it can perform checks on: changes on the data, if changes are authorised or not, and when those changes have been performed. By ensuring this, digital public services can provide additional trust in the data and information provided to stakeholders.&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:concept&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:iopDimension&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;Behavioral IoP&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:view&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;Technical view - application&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:viewpoint&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;Interoperability Security viewpoint&quot;}]}</ns0:properties>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/InteroperabilityFrameworkBusinessObject">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Definition: Interoperability Framework ABB is a Business Object that enables interoperability to organisations that wish to collaborate towards the joint delivery of public services. Within its scope of applicability, it specifies a set of common elements such as vocabulary, concepts, principles, guidelines, and recommendations.

Source: ISA2, EIFv2

Source reference: (&lt;a href=&quot;https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/isa2_en&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/isa2_en&lt;/a&gt;)

Example: The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): The new European Interoperability Framework (EIF) - The new European Interoperability Framework (EIF) is part of the Communication (COM(2017)134) from the European Commission adopted on 23 March 2017. The framework gives specific guidance on how to set up interoperable digital public services. It offers public administrations 47 concrete recommendations on how to improve governance of their interoperability activities, establish cross-organisational relationships, streamline processes supporting end-to-end digital services, and ensure that both existing and new legislation do not compromise interoperability efforts. The new EIF is undertaken in the context of the Commission priority to create a Digital Single Market in Europe. The public sector, which accounts for over a quarter of total employment and represents approximately a fifth of the EU’s GDP through public procurement, plays a key role in the Digital Single Market as a regulator, services provider and employer. The successful implementation of the EIF will improve the quality of European public services and will create an environment where public administrations can collaborate digitally. (&lt;a href=&quot;https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/eif_en&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/eif_en&lt;/a&gt;)

IoP Dimension: Governance IoP

LOST view: Organisational view

Interoperability saliency: The Interoperability Framework ABB is salient for organizational interoperability because it determines a set of rules, practices and a commonly agreed approach to the delivery of European public services.

Identifier: &lt;a href=&quot;http://data.europa.eu/dr8/InteroperabilityFrameworkBusinessObject&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;http://data.europa.eu/dr8/InteroperabilityFrameworkBusinessObject&lt;/a&gt;

eira:ID: ABB206

ABB name: eira:InteroperabilityFrameworkBusinessObject

EIRA concept: eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2022-12-01</skos:definition>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Interoperability Framework</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/viewpoint/InteroperabilityGovernanceViewpoint"/>
    <ns0:properties rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">{&quot;namespaces&quot;:{&quot;rdf&quot;:{&quot;namespace&quot;:&quot;rdf:&quot;,&quot;uri&quot;:&quot;http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1999\/02\/22-rdf-syntax-ns#&quot;},&quot;skos&quot;:{&quot;namespace&quot;:&quot;skos:&quot;,&quot;uri&quot;:&quot;http:\/\/www.w3.org\/2004\/02\/skos\/core#&quot;},&quot;dct&quot;:{&quot;namespace&quot;:&quot;dct:&quot;,&quot;uri&quot;:&quot;http:\/\/purl.org\/dc\/terms\/&quot;},&quot;eira&quot;:{&quot;namespace&quot;:&quot;eira:&quot;,&quot;uri&quot;:&quot;http:\/\/data.europa.eu\/dr8\/&quot;}},&quot;rows&quot;:[{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;rdf:type&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;http:\/\/www.w3.org\/2004\/02\/skos\/core#Concept&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;skos:notation&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;Properties of Interoperability Framework&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;dct:identifier&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;http:\/\/data.europa.eu\/dr8\/InteroperabilityFrameworkBusinessObject_Properties&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;dct:identifier&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;http:\/\/data.europa.eu\/dr8\/InteroperabilityFrameworkBusinessObject&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;skos:prefLabel&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;Properties of Interoperability Framework&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:PURI&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;http:\/\/data.europa.eu\/dr8\/InteroperabilityFrameworkBusinessObject&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;dct:type&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;eira:InteroperabilityFrameworkBusinessObject&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;dct:modified&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;2022-12-1&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;skos:definition&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;Interoperability Framework ABB is a Business Object that enables interoperability to organisations that wish to collaborate towards the joint delivery of public services. Within its scope of applicability, it specifies a set of common elements such as vocabulary, concepts, principles, guidelines, and recommendations.&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:definitionSource&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;ISA2, EIFv2&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:definitionSourceReference&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;(https:\/\/ec.europa.eu\/isa2\/isa2_en)&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;skos:example&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): The new European Interoperability Framework (EIF) - The new European Interoperability Framework (EIF) is part of the Communication (COM(2017)134) from the European Commission adopted on 23 March 2017. The framework gives specific guidance on how to set up interoperable digital public services. It offers public administrations 47 concrete recommendations on how to improve governance of their interoperability activities, establish cross-organisational relationships, streamline processes supporting end-to-end digital services, and ensure that both existing and new legislation do not compromise interoperability efforts. The new EIF is undertaken in the context of the Commission priority to create a Digital Single Market in Europe. The public sector, which accounts for over a quarter of total employment and represents approximately a fifth of the EU\u2019s GDP through public procurement, plays a key role in the Digital Single Market as a regulator, services provider and employer. The successful implementation of the EIF will improve the quality of European public services and will create an environment where public administrations can collaborate digitally. (https:\/\/ec.europa.eu\/isa2\/eif_en)&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:iopSaliency&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;The Interoperability Framework ABB is salient for organizational interoperability because it determines a set of rules, practices and a commonly agreed approach to the delivery of European public services.&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:concept&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:iopDimension&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;Governance IoP&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:view&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;Organisational view&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:viewpoint&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;Interoperability Governance viewpoint&quot;}]}</ns0:properties>
