  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/PrivateCloudFacility">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Definition: Private Cloud Computing Facility ABB is a Facility that enables a cloud infrastructure that is exclusively dedicated to a single organization or user.

Source: Inspired in Redhat

Source reference: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.redhat.com/en/topics/cloud-computing/public-cloud-vs-private-cloud-and-hybrid-cloud&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://www.redhat.com/en/topics/cloud-computing/public-cloud-vs-privat…&lt;/a&gt;

Example: The following implementation is an example of how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): JRC- Development of the EU Green Public Procurement (GPP)- Critaria for Data Centres, Server Rooms and Cloud Services. &lt;a href=&quot;https://ec.europa.eu/environment/gpp/pdf/jrc118558_2020_0605_data_centres_technical_report_jrc_clean_with_id.pdf&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://ec.europa.eu/environment/gpp/pdf/jrc118558_2020_0605_data_centr…&lt;/a&gt;

LOST view: Technical view - Infrastructure

Interoperability saliency: Private Cloud Facilities ABB is salient for organizational and technical interoperability because it establishes the business rules and responsibilities to expose public digital services that are restricted for the use of custom organizations, users or devices.

Identifier: &lt;a href=&quot;http://data.europa.eu/dr8/PrivateCloudFacility&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;http://data.europa.eu/dr8/PrivateCloudFacility&lt;/a&gt;

eira:ID: &lt;a href=&quot;http://data.europa.eu/dr8/PrivateCloudFacility&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;http://data.europa.eu/dr8/PrivateCloudFacility&lt;/a&gt;

ABB name: eira:PrivateCloudFacility

EIRA concept: eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2022-31-01</skos:definition>
